@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Get class
GET http://localhost:8000/api/class
### Get all courses
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses

### Get one course
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses/6a7e8c360efce5962977e1fe

### Filter courses by status
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses?status=ACTIVE

### Filter courses by category
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses?category=Software Engineering

### Filter courses by level
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses?level=Beginner

### Filter courses by capacity
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses?capacity=FULL

### Get Paged courses
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses/paged?page=0&size=5

### Get Paged courses sorted by name ascending
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=title&direction=asc

### Get Paged courses sorted by courseCode descending
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=courseCode&direction=desc

### Get invalid course
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses/999

### Create a new course
POST http://localhost:8000/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "courseCode": "CS104",
    "title": "Introduction to Computer Science",
    "description": "An introductory course on computer science concepts.",
    "category": "Computer Science",
    "level" : "Beginner",
    "capacity": "3 Empty"
}

### Create invalid new course
POST http://localhost:8000/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "courseCode": "",
    "title": "",
    "description": "",
    "category": "",
    "capacity": 0
}


### ======== Check wrong course ==========

### Filter courses by status
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses?status=INVALID

### Get Paged courses
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses/paged?page=0&size=100

### Get Paged courses sorted by name ascending
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=unknownDirection&direction=asc

### Get Paged courses
GET http://localhost:8000/api/courses?status=ACTIVE&level=ADVANCED


### ======== JWT Authenication Tests =========

### Try to access course without token - 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses

### Register a normal student - return token with role student
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name" : "Normal Student",
    "email" : "student@example.com",
    "password" : "Student@12345"
}

### Login normal student
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email" : "student@example.com",
    "password" : "Student@12345"
}

### Try to create course with USER token - return 403 forbidden
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses
Authorization: Bearer STUDENT-TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "courseCode": "SE105",
    "title": "Introduction to C Programming",
    "description": "An Introducy of C Programming.",
    "category": "Programming",
    "level" : "Beginner",
    "capacity": "3 Empty"
}

### Login seeded admin user